so where will it be hosted 

Excellent question!
Where the OSS Self-Healing Agent is hosted depends on your environment and requirements:
1. Kubernetes (K8s) Environment
Hosted in your own Kubernetes cluster (in your cloud account or on-prem).
The agent runs as a container in a pod, typically as a sidecar alongside your self-healing processor container.
You control the namespace, pod, and deployment.
The agent and processor communicate over localhost within the pod.
2. Virtual Server Instance (VSI) / Docker
Hosted on your own virtual machine or server (cloud or on-prem).
The agent runs as a Docker container, alongside your processor container.
You can use Docker Compose or run containers manually.
Both containers communicate over localhost.
3. Who Hosts It?
You (the service team) host the agent in your own environment.
The OSS team provides the agent bundle and support, but does not host it for you.
This ensures security and that the agent has access to your internal monitoring and remediation systems.
4. Where NOT to Host
Do not expose the agent to the public internet.
Do not run the agent in a shared or multi-tenant environment where other teams can access it.
5. Summary Table
Platform	Where Hosted?	Who Manages?
Kubernetes	Your K8s cluster (your pod)	You/Your team
VSI/Docker	Your VM/server (your Docker)	You/Your team
